### Image load/save without a platform parameter preserves the full multi-platform image

Source: https://github.com/docker/docs/blob/main/content/manuals/engine/release-notes/28.md

Engine 28.0 release note for the Docker API (POST /images/{name}/load and GET /images/{name}/get, which back docker image load and docker image save). It states that passing no platform parameter results in loading/saving the full multi-platform image, i.e. the image index and all its platform variants are preserved.

```markdown
- `POST /images/{name}/load` and `GET /images/{name}/get` now supports a `platform` parameter (JSON encoded OCI Platform type) that lets you specify a platform to load/save. Not passing this parameter results in loading/saving the full multi-platform image. [moby/moby#48295](https://github.com/moby/moby/pull/48295)
```

--------------------------------

### containerd image store > Classic image store

Source: https://github.com/docker/docs/blob/main/content/manuals/desktop/features/containerd.md

The classic image store is Docker's legacy storage backend, replaced by the
containerd image store. It doesn't support image indices or manifest lists, so
you can't load multi-platform images locally or build images with attestations.

Most users have no reason to use the classic image store. It's available for
cases where you need to match older behavior or have compatibility
requirements.
